# Documented exceptions for the CI image scan (.github/workflows/image_scan.yml).
# Every entry needs a rationale and a `Revisit:` trigger — enforced by
# spec/code_smells/template_invariants_spec.rb.

# json 2.18.0 still ships INSIDE Ruby 4.0.7 as a default gem (re-checked on the
# 4.0.7 bump); Gemfile.lock pins the fixed json (>= 2.19.2) and Bundler activates
# it at runtime, so the vulnerable copy is dormant until a Ruby patch replaces it.
# Revisit: on the next Ruby 4.0.x patch (bump .tool-versions), or 2026-12-01.
CVE-2026-33210

# Go stdlib v1.27.1 and golang.org/x/net v0.59.0 baked into thruster's
# precompiled binary (0.1.27, the newest release; toolchain read from the
# published x86_64-linux binary). Three denial-of-service findings, all fixed
# only in Go 1.27.2 (stdlib) and x/net 0.60.0: crafted-HTTP net/http (78667),
# net/http/internal/http2 and x/net/http2 (78669), crypto/tls (97031). No
# thruster release built on the fixed versions exists, so there is no action
# available to us regardless of reachability. The eight go1.26.5-era entries
# this block held were cleared by 0.1.27's go1.27.1 build, their Revisit
# trigger, and removed; the image scan on that change is the proof.
# Revisit: on the next thruster release (> 0.1.27), or 2026-11-15.
CVE-2026-78667
CVE-2026-78669
CVE-2026-97031
